{"id":"mahabharata-11-016","work":"mahabharata","part":11,"partName":"स्त्रीपर्व","partNameEn":"Stri Parva","unit":16,"title":"षोडशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 16 · The women among the dead","summary":{"en":"Krishna leads the weeping women, with Dhritarashtra and Gandhari, to the battlefield, where they see the dead. The women, who had never seen the sun, lie among their husbands' bodies, among jackals, vultures and ravens.","kn":"ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅಳುತ್ತಿರುವ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರನ್ನು, ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ, ಗಾಂಧಾರಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ, ರಣರಂಗಕ್ಕೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವರು ಹತರನ್ನು ನೋಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸೂರ್ಯನನ್ನೇ ಕಾಣದ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರು ನರಿ, ರಣಹದ್ದು, ಕಾಗೆಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಗಂಡಂದಿರ ಶವಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಬಿದ್ದಿದ್ದಾರೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण रोती स्त्रियों को, धृतराष्ट्र और गान्धारी सहित, रणभूमि में ले जाते हैं जहाँ वे मृतकों को देखती हैं। जिन स्त्रियों ने कभी सूर्य नहीं देखा था, वे सियारों, गिद्धों और कौओं के बीच अपने पतियों के शवों में पड़ी हैं।","te":"కృష్ణుడు ఏడుస్తున్న స్త్రీలను, ధృతరాష్ట్ర గాంధారులతో కలిసి రణభూమికి తీసుకెళతాడు; వారు హతులను చూస్తారు. సూర్యుని చూడని స్త్రీలు నక్కలు, గద్దలు, కాకుల మధ్య భర్తల శవాల మధ్య పడి ఉన్నారు.","ta":"கண்ணன் அழும் பெண்களைத் த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் காந்தாரியுடன் களத்துக்கு அழைத்துச் செல்ல, அவர்கள் மாண்டோரைக் காண்கின்றனர். சூரியனையே கண்டிராத பெண்கள் நரி, கழுகு, காக்கைகளிடையே கணவரின் உடல்களிடையே கிடக்கின்றனர்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണൻ കരയുന്ന സ്ത്രീകളെയും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരെയും ഗാന്ധാരിയെയും യുദ്ധക്കളത്തിലേക്ക് നയിക്കുന്നു; അവിടെ അവർ മരിച്ചവരെ കാണുന്നു. ഒരിക്കലും സൂര്യനെ കണ്ടിട്ടില്ലാത്ത സ്ത്രീകൾ, ചുറുക്കന്മാരും കഴുകന്മാരും കാക്കകളും നിറഞ്ഞ ഭർത്താക്കന്മാരുടെ ശരീരങ്ങൾക്കിടയിൽ കിടക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 11.16; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 17 2017","sections":[{"title":"स्त्रीविलापपर्व","titleEn":"Strivilapa Parva (Lament of the women)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु गान्धारी कुरूणामाविकर्तनम् ।\nअपश्यत्तत्र तिष्ठन्ती सर्वं दिव्येन चक्षुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, Gandhari, standing there, saw everything with her divine sight, the destroyer of the Kurus."}},{"n":2,"text":"पतिव्रता महाभागा समानव्रतचारिणी ।\nउग्रेण तपसा युक्ता सततं सत्यवादिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was a devoted wife, greatly fortunate, observing the same vows as her husband, joined to fierce austerity and always truthful."}},{"n":3,"text":"वरदानेन कृष्णस्य महर्षेः पुण्यकर्मणः ।\nदिव्यज्ञानबलोपेता विविधं पर्यदेवयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the boon of the great sage Krishna Dvaipayana, of holy deeds, she had the power of divine knowledge, and she lamented in many ways."}},{"n":4,"text":"ददर्श सा बुद्धिमती दूरादपि यथान्तिके ।\nरणाजिरं नृवीराणामद्भुतं लोमहर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise woman saw from afar, as if near, the wondrous and hair-raising field of battle strewn with great heroes."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्थिकेशपरिस्तीर्णं शोणितौघपरिप्लुतम् ।\nशरीरैर्बहुसाहस्रैर्विनिकीर्णं समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was spread with bones and hair, awash with floods of blood, and scattered everywhere with many thousands of bodies."}},{"n":6,"text":"गजाश्वरथयोधानामावृतं रुधिराविलैः ।\nशरीरैरशिरस्कैश्च विदेहैश्च शिरोगणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was covered with the blood-soaked bodies of elephant, horse and chariot warriors, with headless trunks and heaps of heads cut from bodies."}},{"n":7,"text":"गजाश्वनरवीराणां निःसत्त्वैरभिसंवृतम् ।\nसृगालबडकाकोलकङ्ककाकनिषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was crowded with lifeless heroes, elephants, horses and men, and frequented by jackals, herons, crows, kites and other birds."}},{"n":8,"text":"रक्षसां पुरुषादानां मोदनं कुरराकुलम् ।\nअशिवाभिः शिवाभिश्च नादितं गृध्रसेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was a delight to man-eating demons, thronged with ospreys, loud with ill-omened and auspicious jackals, and haunted by vultures."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो व्यासाभ्यनुज्ञातो धृतराष्ट्रो महीपतिः ।\nपाण्डुपुत्राश्च ते सर्वे युधिष्ठिरपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with Vyasa's leave, King Dhritarashtra and all the sons of Pandu led by Yudhishthira,"}},{"n":10,"text":"वासुदेवं पुरस्कृत्य हतबन्धुं च पार्थिवम् ।\nकुरुस्त्रियः समासाद्य जग्मुरायोधनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"putting Vasudeva before them, and the king who had lost his kin, and the women of the Kurus, went to the battlefield."}},{"n":11,"text":"समासाद्य कुरुक्षेत्रं ताः स्त्रियो निहतेश्वराः ।\nअपश्यन्त हतांस्तत्र पुत्रान्भ्रातॄन्पितॄन्पतीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Kurukshetra, those women, whose lords were slain, saw their sons, brothers, fathers and husbands lying slain there."}},{"n":12,"text":"क्रव्यादैर्भक्ष्यमाणान्वै गोमायुबडवायसैः ।\nभूतैः पिशाचै रक्षोभिर्विविधैश्च निशाचरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They saw them being eaten by flesh-eaters, jackals, herons and crows, by spirits, pishachas, demons and various night-roamers."}},{"n":13,"text":"रुद्राक्रीडनिभं दृष्ट्वा तदा विशसनं स्त्रियः ।\nमहार्हेभ्योऽथ यानेभ्यो विक्रोशन्त्यो निपेतिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that slaughter, like the sport of Rudra, the women cried out and fell down from their costly carriages."}},{"n":14,"text":"अदृष्टपूर्वं पश्यन्त्यो दुःखार्ता भरतस्त्रियः ।\nशरीरेष्वस्खलन्नन्या न्यपतंश्चापरा भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Bharata women, afflicted with grief, seeing what they had never seen before, stumbled on the bodies, and others fell to the ground."}},{"n":15,"text":"श्रान्तानां चाप्यनाथानां नासीत्काचन चेतना ।\nपाञ्चालकुरुयोषाणां कृपणं तदभून्महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Exhausted and without protectors, they had no consciousness left. That was a great and pitiful sight of the Panchala and Kuru women."}},{"n":16,"text":"दुःखोपहतचित्ताभिः समन्तादनुनादितम् ।\nदृष्ट्वायोधनमत्युग्रं धर्मज्ञा सुबलात्मजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that terrible battlefield echoing all around with the cries of those whose hearts were struck by grief, Gandhari, the daughter of Subala, knower of dharma,"}},{"n":17,"text":"ततः सा पुण्डरीकाक्षमामन्त्र्य पुरुषोत्तमम् ।\nकुरूणां वैशसं दृष्ट्वा दुःखाद्वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"then addressed the lotus-eyed best of men, Krishna, and, seeing the destruction of the Kurus, spoke to him in her sorrow."}},{"n":18,"text":"पश्यैताः पुण्डरीकाक्ष स्नुषा मे निहतेश्वराः ।\nप्रकीर्णकेशाः क्रोशन्तीः कुररीरिव माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, lotus-eyed Madhava, at these daughters-in-law of mine, whose lords are slain, crying out like ospreys with disheveled hair."}},{"n":19,"text":"अमूस्त्वभिसमागम्य स्मरन्त्यो भरतर्षभान् ।\nपृथगेवाभ्यधावन्त पुत्रान्भ्रातॄन्पितॄन्पतीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming together and remembering those bulls of the Bharatas, they run, each by herself, to their sons, brothers, fathers and husbands."}},{"n":20,"text":"वीरसूभिर्महाबाहो हतपुत्राभिरावृतम् ।\nक्वचिच्च वीरपत्नीभिर्हतवीराभिराकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The field is crowded with mothers of heroes whose sons are dead, and in places with the wives of heroes whose husbands are slain, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":21,"text":"शोभितं पुरुषव्याघ्रैर्भीष्मकर्णाभिमन्युभिः ।\nद्रोणद्रुपदशल्यैश्च ज्वलद्भिरिव पावकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned by tigers among men, Bhishma, Karna and Abhimanyu, and by Drona, Drupada and Shalya, who blazed like fires."}},{"n":22,"text":"काञ्चनैः कवचैर्निष्कैर्मणिभिश्च महात्मनाम् ।\nअङ्गदैर्हस्तकेयूरैः स्रग्भिश्च समलंकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned with golden armor, necklaces and jewels of the great-souled, with armlets, bracelets and garlands."}},{"n":23,"text":"वीरबाहुविसृष्टाभिः शक्तिभिः परिघैरपि ।\nखड्गैश्च विमलैस्तीक्ष्णैः सशरैश्च शरासनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strewn with spears and iron clubs hurled by heroes' arms, with bright sharp swords, with arrows and bows,"}},{"n":24,"text":"क्रव्यादसंघैर्मुदितैस्तिष्ठद्भिः सहितैः क्वचित् ।\nक्वचिदाक्रीडमानैश्च शयानैरपरैः क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"in places crowded with delighted flesh-eating hordes standing together, in places with others playing, and in places with others lying down."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतदेवंविधं वीर संपश्यायोधनं विभो ।\nपश्यमाना च दह्यामि शोकेनाहं जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, lord, behold such a battlefield. Seeing it, Janardana, I burn with grief."}},{"n":26,"text":"पाञ्चालानां कुरूणां च विनाशं मधुसूदन ।\nपञ्चानामिव भूतानां नाहं वधमचिन्तयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, I never thought that the destruction of the Panchalas and Kurus could be like the slaying of the five elements."}},{"n":27,"text":"तान्सुपर्णाश्च गृध्राश्च निष्कर्षन्त्यसृगुक्षितान् ।\nनिगृह्य कवचेषूग्रा भक्षयन्ति सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eagles and vultures drag them away, drenched in blood, and fiercely tear the armor from them and eat them by the thousands."}},{"n":28,"text":"जयद्रथस्य कर्णस्य तथैव द्रोणभीष्मयोः ।\nअभिमन्योर्विनाशं च कश्चिन्तयितुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who could even imagine the death of Jayadratha, Karna, Drona, Bhishma and Abhimanyu?"}},{"n":29,"text":"अवध्यकल्पान्निहतान्दृष्ट्वाहं मधुसूदन ।\nगृध्रकङ्कबडश्येनश्वसृगालादनीकृतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, I see the slain, who seemed nearly invulnerable, made the food of vultures, herons, crows, hawks, dogs and jackals."}},{"n":30,"text":"अमर्षवशमापन्नान्दुर्योधनवशे स्थितान् ।\nपश्येमान्पुरुषव्याघ्रान्संशान्तान्पावकानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"See these tigers among men, now quenched like fires, who in anger stood under Duryodhana's sway."}},{"n":31,"text":"शयनान्युचिताः सर्वे मृदूनि विमलानि च ।\nविपन्नास्तेऽद्य वसुधां विवृतामधिशेरते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They who were accustomed to soft, spotless beds now lie on the bare earth, fallen in death."}},{"n":32,"text":"बन्दिभिः सततं काले स्तुवद्भिरभिनन्दिताः ।\nशिवानामशिवा घोराः शृण्वन्ति विविधा गिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They who were always praised at the proper times by bards and delighted in it now hear the many ill-omened cries of jackals."}},{"n":33,"text":"ये पुरा शेरते वीराः शयनेषु यशस्विनः ।\nचन्दनागुरुदिग्धाङ्गास्तेऽद्य पांसुषु शेरते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The famed heroes who once lay on beds, their limbs smeared with sandal and aloe, now lie in the dust."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेषामाभरणान्येते गृध्रगोमायुवायसाः ।\nआक्षिपन्त्यशिवा घोरा विनदन्तः पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vultures, jackals and crows pull at their ornaments, screeching terribly again and again."}},{"n":35,"text":"चापानि विशिखान्पीतान्निस्त्रिंशान्विमला गदाः ।\nयुद्धाभिमानिनः प्रीता जीवन्त इव बिभ्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Proud of their fighting, delighted, they still hold their bows, arrows, swords and bright maces as if alive."}},{"n":36,"text":"सुरूपवर्णा बहवः क्रव्यादैरवघट्टिताः ।\nऋषभप्रतिरूपाक्षाः शेरते हरितस्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many of fair form and color, torn by flesh-eaters, lie with eyes like bulls' and with green garlands."}},{"n":37,"text":"अपरे पुनरालिङ्ग्य गदाः परिघबाहवः ।\nशेरतेऽभिमुखाः शूरा दयिता इव योषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others embrace their maces, their arms like iron bars, and lie facing them, brave men like beloved women."}},{"n":38,"text":"बिभ्रतः कवचान्यन्ये विमलान्यायुधानि च ।\nन धर्षयन्ति क्रव्यादा जीवन्तीति जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, bearing armor and bright weapons, are not touched by the flesh-eaters, Janardana, as if they were alive."}},{"n":39,"text":"क्रव्यादैः कृष्यमाणानामपरेषां महात्मनाम् ।\nशातकौम्भ्यः स्रजश्चित्रा विप्रकीर्णाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of other great-souled men dragged by flesh-eaters, the many-colored golden garlands are scattered everywhere."}},{"n":40,"text":"एते गोमायवो भीमा निहतानां यशस्विनाम् ।\nकण्ठान्तरगतान्हारानाक्षिपन्ति सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These fearsome jackals pull by the thousands the necklaces on the throats of those renowned dead."}},{"n":41,"text":"सर्वेष्वपररात्रेषु याननन्दन्त बन्दिनः ।\nस्तुतिभिश्च परार्ध्याभिरुपचारैश्च शिक्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bards who delighted them every late night, trained in praises and the finest services,"}},{"n":42,"text":"तानिमाः परिदेवन्ति दुःखार्ताः परमाङ्गनाः ।\nकृपणं वृष्णिशार्दूल दुःखशोकार्दिता भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"are now bewailed by these excellent women in their grief, piteously, tiger of the Vrishnis, sorely oppressed with sorrow."}},{"n":43,"text":"रक्तोत्पलवनानीव विभान्ति रुचिराणि वै ।\nमुखानि परमस्त्रीणां परिशुष्काणि केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The faces of these noble women, dried up, still shine lovely like beds of red lotuses, Keshava."}},{"n":44,"text":"रुदितोपरता ह्येता ध्यायन्त्यः संपरिप्लुताः ।\nकुरुस्त्रियोऽभिगच्छन्ति तेन तेनैव दुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ceasing from weeping and brooding, flooded with sorrow, the Kuru women go each to the particular dead one who grieves them."}},{"n":45,"text":"एतान्यादित्यवर्णानि तपनीयनिभानि च ।\nरोषरोदनताम्राणि वक्त्राणि कुरुयोषिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These faces of the Kuru women, bright as the sun and like gold, are reddened by anger and weeping."}},{"n":46,"text":"आसामपरिपूर्णार्थं निशम्य परिदेवितम् ।\nइतरेतरसंक्रन्दान्न विजानन्ति योषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing their lament, which cannot fully express their loss, the women do not recognize one another's cries."}},{"n":47,"text":"एता दीर्घमिवोच्छ्वस्य विक्रुश्य च विलप्य च ।\nविस्पन्दमाना दुःखेन वीरा जहति जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some, as if sighing long, crying out and lamenting, writhing in sorrow, give up their lives with their heroes."}},{"n":48,"text":"बह्व्यो दृष्ट्वा शरीराणि क्रोशन्ति विलपन्ति च ।\nपाणिभिश्चापरा घ्नन्ति शिरांसि मृदुपाणयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many, seeing the bodies, cry and lament, and others, soft-handed, strike their heads with their hands."}},{"n":49,"text":"शिरोभिः पतितैर्हस्तैः सर्वाङ्गैर्यूथशः कृतैः ।\nइतरेतरसंपृक्तैराकीर्णा भाति मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth shines scattered with fallen heads, arms and limbs, cut into heaps and mingled together."}},{"n":50,"text":"विशिरस्कानथो कायान्दृष्ट्वा घोराभिनन्दिनः ।\nमुह्यन्त्यनुचिता नार्यो विदेहानि शिरांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing headless bodies and bodiless heads, the women, unaccustomed to it, are bewildered, though some frightfully rejoice in it."}},{"n":51,"text":"शिरः कायेन संधाय प्रेक्षमाणा विचेतसः ।\nअपश्यन्त्यो परं तत्र नेदमस्येति दुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fitting a head to a body, they gaze distraught and, grieving, do not see it, and say, \"This is not his.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"बाहूरुचरणानन्यान्विशिखोन्मथितान्पृथक् ।\nसंदधत्योऽसुखाविष्टा मूर्छन्त्येताः पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gathering separately arms, thighs and feet torn apart by arrows, they are seized with misery and faint again and again."}},{"n":53,"text":"उत्कृत्तशिरसश्चान्यान्विजग्धान्मृगपक्षिभिः ।\nदृष्ट्वा काश्चिन्न जानन्ति भर्तॄन्भरतयोषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing others whose heads are cut off and who are eaten by beasts and birds, some of the Bharata women do not recognize their husbands."}},{"n":54,"text":"पाणिभिश्चापरा घ्नन्ति शिरांसि मधुसूदन ।\nप्रेक्ष्य भ्रातॄन्पितॄन्पुत्रान्पतींश्च निहतान्परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, others strike their heads with their hands, seeing brothers, fathers, sons and husbands killed by enemies."}},{"n":55,"text":"बाहुभिश्च सखड्गैश्च शिरोभिश्च सकुण्डलैः ।\nअगम्यकल्पा पृथिवी मांसशोणितकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With arms and swords and heads with earrings, the earth, a mire of flesh and blood, is almost impassable."}},{"n":56,"text":"न दुःखेषूचिताः पूर्वं दुःखं गाहन्त्यनिन्दिताः ।\nभ्रातृभिः पितृभिः पुत्रैरुपकीर्णां वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These blameless women, not used to suffering before, now plunge into grief, seeing the earth strewn with brothers, fathers and sons."}},{"n":57,"text":"यूथानीव किशोरीणां सुकेशीनां जनार्दन ।\nस्नुषाणां धृतराष्ट्रस्य पश्य वृन्दान्यनेकशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Janardana, at the many bands of Dhritarashtra's daughters-in-law, fair-haired, like herds of young girls."}},{"n":58,"text":"अतो दुःखतरं किं नु केशव प्रतिभाति मे ।\nयदिमाः कुर्वते सर्वा रूपमुच्चावचं स्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What seems to me more painful than this, Keshava, that all these women take on such varied forms of grief?"}},{"n":59,"text":"नूनमाचरितं पापं मया पूर्वेषु जन्मसु ।\nया पश्यामि हतान्पुत्रान्पौत्रान्भ्रातॄंश्च केशव ।\nएवमार्ता विलपती ददर्श निहतं सुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely I did evil in former births, since I see my sons, grandsons and brothers slain, Keshava. Lamenting thus in distress, she saw her slain son."}}]}]}